    content: `<p>Half-yearly exams are approaching, and it is time to get serious about preparation. These exams cover the first half of the syllabus and are crucial for building a strong foundation for the final board exams. Here is a complete preparation guide for students.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Half-Yearly Exam Schedule (Expected)</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Class</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Expected Dates</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Syllabus Coverage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Class 9-10</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">September 15-30, 2026</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">First 4-5 chapters per subject</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Class 11-12</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">September 20 – October 5, 2026</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">First 50% syllabus</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Class 6-8</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">September 10-25, 2026</td><td class="py-3 px-4">First term syllabus</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Subject-wise Preparation Tips</h2>
<p><strong>Mathematics:</strong> Practice daily — at least 20 problems per day. Focus on NCERT examples and exercises. Make a formula sheet for quick revision.</p>
<p><strong>Science:</strong> Understand concepts, don't memorize. Practice diagrams (Biology). Solve numerical problems (Physics). Learn chemical equations (Chemistry).</p>
<p><strong>English:</strong> Read literature chapters thoroughly. Practice writing skills — letters, articles, reports. Grammar rules need daily practice.</p>
<p><strong>Social Science:</strong> Make timeline charts for History. Practice map work for Geography. Understand concepts for Civics and Economics.</p>
<p><strong>Hindi:</strong> Read all chapters. Practice essay writing and letter formats. Grammar (Vyakaran) needs consistent practice.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">30-Day Study Plan for Half-Yearly</h2>
<p><strong>Week 1 (Aug 15-21):</strong> Cover pending syllabus for all subjects. Make notes for each chapter.</p>
<p><strong>Week 2 (Aug 22-28):</strong> Solve previous year half-yearly papers. Identify weak areas.</p>
<p><strong>Week 3 (Aug 29-Sep 4):</strong> Focus on weak topics. Take subject-wise tests.</p>
<p><strong>Week 4 (Sep 5-14):</strong> Full revision. Take mock tests daily. Revise short notes.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Common Mistakes to Avoid</h2>
<p><strong>1. Starting too late:</strong> Don't wait until the last week. Start preparation at least 30 days before exams.</p>
<p><strong>2. Ignoring NCERT:</strong> 80% of questions come from NCERT. Read it thoroughly before reference books.</p>
<p><strong>3. Not practicing writing:</strong> Reading is not enough. Practice writing answers to improve speed and presentation.</p>
<p><strong>4. Skipping sleep:</strong> Sleep 7-8 hours daily. Late-night study sessions do more harm than good.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Exam Coaching at JGPS</h3><p>JGPS School Joya provides structured exam preparation with regular tests and doubt-clearing sessions. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>Half-yearly exams for most schools are scheduled for <strong>September-October 2026</strong>. Start your 30-day preparation plan now. Focus on NCERT and previous year papers for best results. Source: CBSE Academic Calendar (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
