    content: `<p>CUET UG 2026 results have been declared, and many students are experiencing post-result anxiety. Whether your score is lower than expected, you are confused about counselling, or worried about university admission — this stress is normal and manageable.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">CUET UG 2026: Result Summary</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Detail</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Information</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Result Date</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">June 23, 2026</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Total Candidates</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">~15 lakh students</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Score Range</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">200-800 (per subject)</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Good Score</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold">700+ (for top universities)</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Website</td><td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold">cuet.nta.nic.in</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Common Causes of Post-Result Anxiety</h2>
<p><strong>1. Score lower than expected:</strong> You studied hard but the score doesn't reflect your effort.</p>
<p><strong>2. Counselling confusion:</strong> Multiple rounds, choice filling, freeze/float/slide — the process is complex.</p>
<p><strong>3. Peer comparison:</strong> Friends with higher scores getting better college options.</p>
<p><strong>4. Parental pressure:</strong> Fear of disappointing parents with your score or college choice.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How to Manage Post-Result Stress</h2>
<p><strong>1. Accept your score:</strong> The result is done. Focus on what you can do next — not what you could have done differently.</p>
<p><strong>2. Research alternatives:</strong> CUET is not the only path. State universities, private colleges, and direct admissions are also good options.</p>
<p><strong>3. Talk to someone:</strong> Share your feelings with parents, friends, or a counselor. Bottling up stress makes it worse.</p>
<p><strong>4. Stay physically active:</strong> Exercise releases endorphins that reduce stress. Even a 30-minute walk helps.</p>
<p><strong>5. Limit social media:</strong> Stop comparing yourself to others on Instagram. Everyone's journey is different.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What If Your Score Is Low?</h2>
<p><strong>Option 1 — Spot counselling:</strong> Many universities have spot counselling rounds for remaining seats. Apply for these.</p>
<p><strong>Option 2 — State universities:</strong> State universities have their own admission process. Some accept CUET scores, others have their own entrance exams.</p>
<p><strong>Option 3 — Private universities:</strong> Good private universities like Ashoka, Shiv Nadar, and OP Jindal have their own admission process.</p>
<p><strong>Option 4 — Gap year:</strong> If you are determined for a specific college, take a gap year and prepare again. But have a clear plan.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">University Guidance</h3><p>JGPS School Joya provides career and university admission guidance. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>CUET UG 2026 results were declared on <strong>June 23, 2026</strong>. Counselling process is ongoing. Many universities have started their own admission processes. Source: NTA (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
