    content: `<p>The National Education Policy (NEP) 2020 is being implemented in phases across India. In 2026, several new changes are being introduced that directly affect students and parents. Here is what you need to know.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Key NEP Changes in 2026</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Change</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Details</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Impact</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Three-Language Policy</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Students must learn 3 languages until Class 10</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">All CBSE schools</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Board Exam Reform</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Two board exams per year for Class 10</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Class 10 students</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Vocational Training</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Mandatory vocational subject from Class 6</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">All schools</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Coding & AI</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Coding and AI introduced from Class 6</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">CBSE schools</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Assessment Reform</td><td class="py-3 px-4">Continuous assessment, not just final exams</td><td class="py-3 px-4">All schools</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Three-Language Policy: What It Means</h2>
<p>The most discussed change is the three-language policy. Students must learn:</p>
<p><strong>Language 1:</strong> Mother tongue or regional language (mandatory)</p>
<p><strong>Language 2:</strong> English (mandatory)</p>
<p><strong>Language 3:</strong> Hindi or another Indian language (mandatory until Class 10)</p>
<p><strong>Controversy:</strong> This has caused debate, especially in non-Hindi speaking states. Many parents worry about additional academic burden. Some states like Tamil Nadu have opposed the Hindi requirement.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Two Board Exams for Class 10</h2>
<p>From 2026, CBSE Class 10 students can appear for board exams <strong>twice a year</strong>:</p>
<p><strong>First Board (February-March):</strong> Mandatory for all students. Covers full syllabus.</p>
<p><strong>Second Board (May-June):</strong> Optional. Students can improve their score in any subject.</p>
<p><strong>Best of Two:</strong> The higher marks from either attempt are considered for the final marksheet.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Vocational Training from Class 6</h2>
<p>All schools must now offer at least one vocational subject from Class 6. Options include:</p>
<p>• IT and Digital Skills</p>
<p>• Agriculture and Food Processing</p>
<p>• Healthcare and Wellness</p>
<p>• Tourism and Hospitality</p>
<p>• Banking and Finance</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What Parents Should Do</h2>
<p><strong>1. Understand the changes:</strong> Don't panic. Read about NEP from official sources (education.gov.in).</p>
<p><strong>2. Support your child:</strong> The three-language policy adds workload. Help your child manage time effectively.</p>
<p><strong>3. Explore vocational options:</strong> Vocational subjects can lead to career opportunities. Encourage your child to explore.</p>
<p><strong>4. Stay updated:</strong> Follow your school's communication for specific implementation details.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">NEP-Ready Education</h3><p>JGPS School Joya is fully NEP-compliant with modern teaching methods. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for admissions.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>NEP 2020 implementation is progressing across India. The three-language policy has faced opposition in some states. CBSE has issued detailed guidelines for schools. Source: Ministry of Education (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
