    content: `<p>The Feynman Technique, named after Nobel laureate physicist Richard Feynman, is one of the most effective learning methods. For AMU Class 6 Math preparation, this technique can help students truly understand mathematical concepts instead of just memorizing formulas.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What is the Feynman Technique?</h2>
<p>The Feynman Technique has 4 simple steps:</p>
<p><strong>Step 1 — Choose a concept:</strong> Pick a math topic you want to learn (e.g., fractions, percentages, geometry).</p>
<p><strong>Step 2 — Teach it simply:</strong> Explain the concept in simple language as if teaching a 10-year-old. Use plain Hindi or English — no jargon.</p>
<p><strong>Step 3 — Identify gaps:</strong> When you struggle to explain something, that is a gap in your understanding. Go back and study that part.</p>
<p><strong>Step 4 — Simplify and repeat:</strong> Once you can explain the concept simply and clearly, you truly understand it.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Applying Feynman Technique to AMU Math</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Topic</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">How to Apply Feynman Technique</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Fractions</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Explain to a friend: "A fraction is like cutting a pizza into equal pieces"</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Percentages</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">"Percent means per hundred. 50% means 50 out of 100, which is half"</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Geometry</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Draw shapes and explain properties using real-world examples</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">Word Problems</td><td class="py-3 px-4">Break the problem into small steps and explain each step</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Daily Feynman Practice Plan</h2>
<p><strong>Morning (30 min):</strong> Choose 1 math topic. Study it from NCERT.</p>
<p><strong>Afternoon (30 min):</strong> Explain the topic to a family member or imaginary student. Record yourself if possible.</p>
<p><strong>Evening (30 min):</strong> Identify gaps where you struggled. Study those gaps. Explain again.</p>
<p><strong>Result:</strong> After 30 days, you will have mastered 30 math topics with deep understanding.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Why Feynman Technique Works for Math</h2>
<p><strong>1. Forces understanding:</strong> You cannot explain what you don't understand. Teaching exposes gaps.</p>
<p><strong>2. Builds confidence:</strong> When you can explain a concept simply, you feel confident about it.</p>
<p><strong>3. Improves retention:</strong> Teaching others moves information from short-term to long-term memory.</p>
<p><strong>4. Identifies weak areas:</strong> You immediately know which topics need more work.</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Math Coaching at JGPS</h3><p>JGPS School Joya uses the Feynman Technique and other proven methods for AMU entrance preparation. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>AMU Class 6 entrance exam 2027 is expected in <strong>February 2027</strong>. Start using the Feynman Technique now for better math preparation. Source: JGPS Academic Team (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
