    content: `<p>While AISSEE Class 6 admission does not have a formal interview, the counselling process involves document verification and sometimes informal interaction. For Class 9, some schools conduct interviews. Here are common questions and how to prepare.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Common Questions in Sainik School Counselling</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto my-6"><table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-gray-200 shadow-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden text-sm"><thead class="bg-[#035c00]"><tr><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Category</th><th class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-bold text-white text-left">Sample Questions</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Personal</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">What is your name? Where are you from? Tell us about your family.</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Academic</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Which school do you study in? What is your favorite subject? Why?</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Motivation</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">Why do you want to join Sainik School? What do you know about Sainik School?</td></tr><tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b font-medium text-gray-900">Career</td><td class="py-3 px-4 border-b">What do you want to become when you grow up? Why?</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900">General</td><td class="py-3 px-4">Who is the President of India? What is the capital of your state?</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How to Prepare Your Child</h2>
<p><strong>1. Practice speaking:</strong> Encourage your child to speak clearly and confidently. Practice answering questions in front of a mirror.</p>
<p><strong>2. Know about Sainik School:</strong> Your child should know basic facts — how many Sainik Schools, who manages them, what is NDA.</p>
<p><strong>3. Current affairs:</strong> Teach your child basic GK — President, Prime Minister, capital of India, neighboring countries.</p>
<p><strong>4. Be honest:</strong> Teach your child to answer honestly. If they don't know something, it is okay to say "I don't know."</p>
<p><strong>5. Body language:</strong> Sit straight, make eye contact, speak clearly, and smile. Good body language creates a positive impression.</p>

<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Sample Answers</h2>
<p><strong>Q: Why do you want to join Sainik School?</strong></p>
<p>A: "I want to join Sainik School because I want to serve my country. I admire the discipline and values that Sainik School teaches. I also want to prepare for NDA and become an army officer."</p>

<p><strong>Q: What is your favorite subject?</strong></p>
<p>A: "My favorite subject is Mathematics because I enjoy solving problems. I also like Science because it helps me understand how things work."</p>

<p><strong>Q: What do you want to become?</strong></p>
<p>A: "I want to become an army officer and serve my country. Sainik School will help me prepare for NDA."</p>

<div class="bg-[#035c00]/5 border border-[#035c00]/20 rounded-xl p-5 my-6"><h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Interview Preparation at JGPS</h3><p>JGPS School Joya prepares students for Sainik School counselling and interviews. Call <strong>+91 9412137554</strong> for details.</p></div>

<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
<h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">August 2026 Update</h3>
<p>AISSEE 2027 counselling process will include document verification. Prepare your child for basic questions about themselves and Sainik School. Source: Sainik School Society (August 2026).</p>
</div>`,
